  "id": "COMPOUND:30070 - PROTEIN:5839",
  "verbalization": "Hippurin-1 is implicated in the biological pathway leading to U251 through multiple intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Hippurin-1 directly targets Raji, which in turn is targeted by Maplexin A and 7-Angeloylechinatine, all of which ultimately interact with U251. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Hippurin-1 may act as a central node in the network, influencing the activity of these downstream targets. The presence of multiple distinct targets (Raji, Maplexin A, and VMRC-LCP) suggests that Hippurin-1 may exert its effects through different mechanisms, potentially involving diverse molecular pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Hippurin-1 and U251, with the possibility of multiple layers of regulation and interaction.",
